+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent sets toolChoice to 'required', so after approveRefund returns approved: false the model is forced to call a tool again (approveRefund) and can never produce the final text reply to the customer.",
+  "evidence": "Reproduced with a scripted model that enforces toolChoice: after the decline response, every model call carried toolChoice=required and the only legal output was another approveRefund interrupt, so the turn stayed 'interrupted' with empty text on each resume; changing the agent to toolChoice 'auto' in the same harness made the post-decline call return a text reply with finishReason 'stop'."
+}
